520
00:29:31,830 --> 00:29:38,730
Maya: Yeah, and the IEA projects 26 million km of new lines by 2035 to keep pace.

521
00:29:39,300 --> 00:29:41,210
Alex: Sounds like a grid‑expansion marathon.

522
00:29:41,670 --> 00:29:47,510
Maya: The report also notes renewable growth will jump 85 % over the next decade—solar to

523
00:29:47,510 --> 00:29:50,140
Maya: dominate past the late 2030s.

524
00:29:50,540 --> 00:29:52,890
Alex: So the grid’s getting a renewable makeover too?

525
00:29:53,230 --> 00:30:00,020
Maya: Exactly, and electricity could hit 30 % of global final energy use by 2035,

526
00:30:00,020 --> 00:30:02,650
Maya: up from 23 % in baseline scenarios.

527
00:30:03,310 --> 00:30:06,670
Maya: The grid race feels like a sprint where the finish line keeps moving.

528
00:30:07,250 --> 00:30:11,390
Alex: But the tech side worries about how soon those lines can actually be laid.

529
00:30:11,920 --> 00:30:14,290
